PROGRAM – 8

TITLE: Set up a Jenkins CI Pipeline for a Maven Project and Deploy Artifacts using Ansible

AIM:
To set up a Jenkins CI pipeline for a Maven project and deploy the generated artifacts using Ansible.

PROCEDURE:

1. Install Ubuntu (WSL).

   wsl --install

2. Update the system.

   sudo apt update

3. Install Java JDK 17.

   sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk -y

4. Verify Java installation.

   java -version
   javac -version

5. Install Maven.

   sudo apt install maven -y

6. Verify Maven installation.

   mvn -version

7. Install Jenkins.

   wget https://get.jenkins.io/war-stable/latest/jenkins.war

8. Run Jenkins.

   java -jar jenkins.war

9. Open Jenkins in browser.

   http://localhost:8080

10. Obtain Jenkins password.

    cat ~/.jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

11. Install Ansible.

    sudo apt install ansible -y

12. Verify Ansible installation.

    ansible --version

13. Install SSH Server.

    sudo apt install openssh-server -y

14. Start SSH service.

    sudo systemctl start ssh
    sudo systemctl enable ssh

15. Configure passwordless SSH.

    ssh-keygen
    ssh-copy-id $(whoami)@localhost
    ssh localhost

16. Create Ansible inventory file.

    nano hosts

    Add:

    [servers]
    localhost ansible_connection=local

17. Test Ansible connectivity.

    ansible all -i hosts -m ping

OUTPUT:

```text
localhost | SUCCESS
{
    "ping": "pong"
}
```

RESULT:
Successfully configured Jenkins CI pipeline for a Maven project and verified deployment connectivity using Ansible.
